  "problem": "Let\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}].$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$",
  "worked_solution": "We notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2\\times 4:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 4}={BA}_{2\\times 4}\n$$",
